<title>TUNISIA: Tunisia, South Africa sign air transport accord.</title>
<headline>Tunisia, South Africa sign air transport accord.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tunisia and South Africa have signed an accord establishing the legal framework for air links between the two countries, officials said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The accord allows scheduled flights and transit advantages for their airlines to increase trade and tourist exchanges between the south and the north of the African continent, they added.</p>
<p>The accord was signed by Tunisian Prime Minister Hamed Karoui and South African Deputy President Thabo Mbeki, who arrived on Wednesday in Tunis for a three-day visit.</p>
